\" by Clayton Kroh. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 30 Apr 2014."}},{"id":"thank-gods-2014-04-30-e3","summary":"Raissa decides not to abandon her child to Setessa as most satyr women would, believing he is special and needs her.","participants":["raissa","xenagos","setessan-order-of-midwives"],"location":"setessa","importance":"minor","page":"stories/thank-gods-2014-04-30","order":28,"story_date":"2014-04-30","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":13,"quote":"This child was special, and he would need her to fulfill the destiny she had witnessed.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/thank-gods-2014-04-30#:~:text=This%20child%20was%20special%2C,destiny%20she%20had%20witnessed.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Thank the Gods","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Clayton Kroh"],"date":"2014-04-30","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/thank-gods-2014-04-30","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/thank-gods-2014-04-30#:~:text=This%20child%20was%20special%2C,destiny%20she%20had%20witnessed.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Thank the Gods\" by Clayton Kroh. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 30 Apr 2014."}},{"id":"thank-gods-2014-04-30-e4","summary":"Years later, Raissa escapes a burning house with her six-year-old son, who set her bed alight; they have been cast out of Setessa after he pushed a council member's son to his death.","participants":["raissa","xenagos","setessa","karametra"],"location":"setessa","importance":"major","page":"stories/thank-gods-2014-04-30","order":28,"story_date":"2014-04-30","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":15,"quote":"He had caused them to be cast out of Setessa when he shoved the son of one of the Karametra temple's ruling council to his death from a high rope bridge among the trees.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/thank-gods-2014-04-30#:~:text=He%20had%20caused%20them,bridge%20among%20